    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31575" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏb-armo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to arm</i> (<b>poet.</b>
			and post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">securi Dextras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 4, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clipeo filium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 25, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus impias contra aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perfrictis oculis, et obarmatis ad vigilias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 125, 28</span></i>
			.</div>
